  "interpretation": "Byte-identical first-10k replay observations/actions/float32 rewards/semantic terminal masks and fixed seed-probe indices/contents establish input-data parity for this source-initialized training phase. Despite that, the first planned action is different before any observed damage-penalty event. No model, optimizer, pixel-augmentation RNG or planner RNG state was frozen at exactly decision 10000. The later 20k checkpoint weights do not reconstruct that state; a source review found no demonstrable extra PRNG call. Causal explanation of the first divergence is UNKNOWN. The treatment is a nominally single-reward-objective source design on matched settings, not matched action/transition learner trajectories; a one-seed finish-rate change cannot be attributed to damage shaping alone. Future raw/raw deterministic seed-boundary snapshot and replicated learner-seed controls would be needed for a causal claim."
